of Silla, Gyeongju, was the primary administrative and cultural center during Jijeung's reign."}, {"sourceSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "sourceName": "Jijeung of Silla", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "soji-of-silla", "targetName": "Soji of Silla", "context": "Jijeung of Silla succeeded King Soji, becoming the 22nd ruler of Silla in 500 CE."}], "places": [{"name": "Gyeongju, South Korea", "role": "Capital City"}, {"name": "Ulleungdo, South Korea", "role": "Conquered Territory"}, {"name": "Korean Peninsula", "role": "Geopolitical Context"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Jijeung of Silla", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "jijeung-of-silla"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q491142", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jijeung_of_Silla"], "tags": ["Monarchs & Rulers", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Jijeung's reign fundamentally transformed Silla from a tribal confederacy into a centralized kingdom, setting the administrative and territorial precedents that enabled its later unification of the Korean Peninsula. His reforms directly led to a stronger state capable of significant expansion.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-08-09T07:01:56Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#31298622523", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Jijeung (437–514) was the 22nd ruler and 1st king of the Koreanic kingdom Silla. He is remembered for strengthening royal authority and building Silla into a centralized kingdom. On the contemporary Naengsuri Silla monument, his name was inscribed as Jidoro.", "newValue": "Jijeung of Silla (437–514 CE) stands as the 22nd ruler and the inaugural monarch of the Koreanic kingdom of Silla, reigning from 500 to 514 CE. His 14-year reign marked a pivotal transition for Silla, transforming it from a loosely organized tribal confederacy into a centralized, expansionist kingdom. He is historically significant for institutionalizing royal authority, establishing foundational administrative frameworks, and initiating the territorial consolidation that would later enable Silla's unification of the Korean Peninsula.

During his rule, Jijeung implemented a series of transformative reforms. In 503 CE, he formally adopted the title of "King" (Wang, 왕), replacing the earlier, less authoritative "Maripgan" and thereby consolidating the monarch's power and legitimizing Silla as a sovereign state. He standardized the measurement system and significantly boosted agricultural productivity by introducing oxen for plowing, a technological advancement with profound economic implications. Militarily, his most notable achievement was the conquest of Usan-guk (modern-day Ulleungdo and Dokdo islands) in 512 CE, expanding Silla's maritime domain and securing vital coastal trade routes. He also established Ushi-san Guk as the kingdom's first administrative division (gun) in 505 CE, signaling an emerging bureaucratic structure.

Jijeung's reforms had profound and lasting consequences, fundamentally reshaping Silla's internal structure and external projection. By centralizing royal power and establishing a more robust administrative and territorial apparatus, he created the necessary conditions for his successors, particularly Beopheung and Jinheung, to pursue aggressive expansion, implement Buddhist statecraft, and achieve cultural assimilation. His reign solidified Silla's identity as a distinct and formidable state, setting the stage for its eventual emergence as the dominant power on the peninsula and paving the way for the Unified Silla period."}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-09T07:01:56Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#31298622523", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "437 CE"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "437 CE"}], "newValue": ["The inherent weakness and decentralized nature of the Silla tribal confederacy necessitated stronger royal authority to compete with neighboring kingdoms.", "The ongoing geopolitical rivalries with Baekje and Goguryeo pressured Silla to develop a more centralized and militarily capable state.", "The existing Silla royal lineage, particularly the Kim clan, sought to consolidate and legitimize its power over other aristocratic factions."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-09T07:01:56Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#31298622523", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "514 CE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "514 CE"}], "newValue": ["Silla transformed into a centralized kingdom with a more robust administrative and military structure capable of sustained expansion.", "The formal adoption of the 'King' title in Silla solidified monarchical power and elevated its international standing among East Asian states.", "The conquest of Usan-guk expanded Silla's territory and maritime influence, setting a precedent for future territorial ambitions."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-09T07:01:56Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#31298622523", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "sourceName": "Jijeung of Silla", "verb": "RULES", "targetSlug": "field-221", "targetName": "Monarchs & Rulers", "context": "Jijeung of Silla: Sovereign authority in monarchs & rulers"}, {"sourceSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "sourceName": "Jijeung of Silla", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "classical", "targetName": "Classical Era", "context": "Jijeung of Silla was active during the Classical era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "sourceName": "Jijeung of Silla", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "silla-kingdom", "targetName": "Silla Kingdom", "context": "Jijeung's reign (500-514 CE) transformed the Silla Kingdom from a tribal confederacy into a centralized monarchy."}, {"sourceSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "sourceName": "Jijeung of Silla", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "unification-of-korean-peninsula", "targetName": "Unification of Korean Peninsula", "context": "Jijeung's foundational reforms and territorial expansion created conditions that ultimately contributed to Silla's later unification of the Korean Peninsula."}, {"sourceSlug": "kim-clan", "sourceName": "Kim Clan", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "targetName": "Jijeung of Silla", "context": "Jijeung's rise to power was influenced by the Kim clan's established dominance within the Silla aristocracy."}, {"sourceSlug": "jijeung-of-silla", "sourceName": "Jijeung of Silla", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "gyeongju-south-korea", "targetName": "Gyeongju, South Korea", "context": "The capital o